    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/70287": {
      "title": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | Assistant Director of Business Services for HRL",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | Assistant Director of Business Services for HRL Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment Assistant Director of Business Services for HRL Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Position Information General Information Position Number 010601 Vacancy Open to All Candidates Working Title Assistant Director of Business Services for HRL Position Designation EHRA Non-Faculty Employment Type Permanent - Full-time Months per Year 12 Work Schedule 8:00 am – 5:00 pm; Monday – Friday Hours per week 40 FLSA Status Exempt Division Student Affairs Department Housing and Residence Life (Adm) Work Location Housing and Residence Life (HRL) building Salary Range $54,249 - $75,000 Primary Purpose of Department Within the Division of Student Affairs, the mission of Housing and Residence Life is to create communities in partnership with residential students that are inclusive, safe, well-maintained, and intentionally developed to facilitate their academic, personal, and professional growth. This department is comprised of four (4) sub-units: Business Services, Facilities Operations, Administration and Assessment, and Residence Life. The Business Services unit is responsible for managing the department’s budget and financial affairs, purchasing activities, and providing general HR support for employees and the management team. Additionally, this unit provides oversight of the residence hall Security Services. Primary Purpose of Position The primary purpose of this position is to support the Director of Business Operations in administering and maintaining the financial and personnel operations of Housing and Residence Life and to provide continuity of divisional business functions as needed. This role performs a broad range of financial and business-related duties associated with budgeting, financial analysis, forecasting, auditing, personnel administration, and compliance within a complex, multi-funded auxiliary environment. The position works directly with Housing and Residence Life unit leaders to ensure financial reports are clear, accessible, and actionable, and provides guidance to help units understand and navigate the budgeting process throughout the fiscal year. This role serves as a liaison to Human Resources and Employee Relations, providing consultation to supervisors on position management, recruitment processes, performance management, and employee conduct matters in accordance with university and state policies. The position works closely with the Business Analyst to ensure smooth student employment onboarding and offboarding processes and supports supervisory needs related to the overnight security team to ensure operational continuity and compliance. Additionally, the role assists with vendor relations, including financial oversight, contract monitoring, essential notifications, and vendor registration processes to support fiscal accountability and operational efficiency. The position must develop and maintain a strong working knowledge of enterprise financial and human resource systems, including but not limited to Banner, NinerTalent, NinerWorks, Concur, and related reporting platforms, in order to effectively support budgeting, personnel transactions, compliance requirements, and divisional reporting needs. Summary of Position Responsibilities The Director of Business Services independently manages a broad range of business functions for Housing and Residence Life, overseeing all financial activities. The director shares in the responsibility for department-level strategic planning and is expected to provide expertise regarding the department’s financial health, long-term staffing and professional development needs, cost-reduction opportunities, and collaborative business partnerships that add value to the department’s programs and services. Minimum Education/Experience Bachelor’s degree in business administration, public administration, or related business area; or Equivalent combination of training and experience. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Preferred Education, Knowledge, Skills and Experience At least 3 years of supervisory and relevant experience within higher education housing or auxiliary service operations. Necessary Certifications/Licenses Preferred Certifications/Licenses Special Notes to Applicants The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist. Please ensure your resume reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Posting Open Date 06/22/2026 Posting Close Date 09/22/2026 Open Until Filled No Proposed Hire Date 08/10/2026 If time-limited please indicate appointment end date Contact Information Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Mitratech Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a bachelor’s degree in business administration, public administration, or a related business area, or an equivalent combination of training and experience? All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Yes, at least a bachelor’s degree in business administration, public administration, or a related business area. Yes, an associate's degree in business administration, public administration, or a related business area and two years of relevant work experience. Yes, a high school diploma and 4 years of relevant work experience. No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Contact Information for References Optional Documents 9201 University City Blvd \r\nCharlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
