    "https://jobs.charlotte.edu/postings/70267": {
      "title": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site",
      "description": "UNC Charlotte Applicant Site | Transfer Advisor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Application Process State of NC Salary Chart Campus Security Report Student Employment Transfer Advisor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. If there is a document you feel is relevant to this position that you would like reviewed with your resume and application, you may upload it to the \"Other Documents\" section of the Applicant Documents. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist . Please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Position Information General Information Position Number 006766 Vacancy Open to All Candidates Working Title Transfer Advisor Position Designation EHRA Non-Faculty Employment Type Permanent - Full-time Months per Year 12 Work Schedule Monday – Friday, 8:00 am – 5:00 pm Hours per week 40 FLSA Status Exempt Division Academic Affairs Department Undergraduate Education (Adm) Work Location UNC Charlotte Salary Range $55,000 - $57,999 Primary Purpose of Department The University Transfer and Adult Student Center provides advising support, transition services, and advocacy to promote transfer and adult student success. Through collaboration with campus and external partners, the Center connects students to the resources, pathways, and support systems that facilitate a smooth transition into the university and support their progression to graduation. The Center serves as a resource to transfer and adult students, with a particular emphasis on prospective and newly enrolled students, as well as a resource to faculty and staff. Primary Purpose of Position The Transfer Advisor supports prospective and enrolled students with prior college credit, including transfer and adult learners, by providing academic advising and transition support. The position will primarily provide pre-transfer advising to students participating in UNC Charlotte’s 49erNext program while also supporting other transfer and adult students based on Center priorities and student needs. The advisor helps students understand how prior coursework may apply to degree requirements, explore academic options, and identify coursework that supports preparation for their intended major and timely progression to graduation. Pre-transfer advising is currently delivered primarily through individual appointments and Transfer Guides. This position will help expand access to advising by developing group sessions and other scalable resources that provide clear and consistent guidance throughout the transfer process. The advisor also contributes to outreach, engagement programming, and collaborative initiatives that strengthen transfer and adult student pathways, improve credit mobility, and support students as they transition to UNC Charlotte. Summary of Position Responsibilities Advising and Student Support (70%) Provide academic advising to prospective and enrolled transfer and adult students through in-person and virtual appointments and other advising modalities. Maintain an assigned caseload of 49erNext students enrolled at North Carolina community colleges and provide proactive pre-transfer advising and follow-up. Assist students in understanding how prior credit may apply to degree requirements, including general education, major prerequisites, and course sequencing. Guide students in exploring academic options and selecting coursework prior to enrollment that supports preparation for their intended major and timely progression toward graduation. Support students in navigating academic policies and processes, including major admission and declaration requirements, change of major processes, and institutional expectations after transfer. Provide supplemental advising support to enrolled students with transfer credit, including guidance on the academic petition process for credit reevaluation. Support newly enrolled students in navigating their transition and connecting with appropriate campus resources and services. Maintain accurate and timely documentation of advising interactions in accordance with university policies and best practices. Resource Development, Outreach, and Engagement (15%) Develop and facilitate group advising sessions, and other scalable opportunities, that expand access to pre-transfer guidance for all prospective UNC Charlotte students, including students participating in 49erNext. Participate in outreach efforts, including partner visits, campus events, and virtual engagement opportunities. Assist with engagement and transition programming for transfer initiatives, including 49erNext Scholars, to help incoming students connect with campus resources, understand academic expectations, and build community. Use student questions, advising trends, participation data, and feedback to identify opportunities for new resources and improvements to advising and programming. Communication and Operational Support (10%) Monitor and respond to inquiries received through Center email accounts and other communication channels. Provide timely, accurate, and student-centered information to prospective and enrolled students. Assist with the development and maintenance of advising resources, program communications, and website content. Support data collection and reporting related to advising, resource use, program participation, and student engagement. Projects, Collaboration, and Professional Development (5%) Participate in departmental and university initiatives related to transfer, adult learner success, student transition, and pathway development. Collaborate with campus and external partners to support transfer pathways, improve the student experience, and reduce credit loss. Serve on committees or working groups as appropriate. Engage in ongoing professional development to stay current with best practices in advising, transfer, and adult student support. Minimum Education/Experience Master’s degree in higher education, student affairs, counseling, or a related field. Preferred Education, Knowledge, Skills and Experience Master’s degree and 1-2 years of direct experience advising, coaching, or counseling college students. Experience working with North Carolina community college or university transfer students. Demonstration of ability to establish rapport with individuals, inspire confidence, and build relationships. Excellent verbal and written communication skills that demonstrate tact, diplomacy, and the maintenance of confidentiality. Necessary Certifications/Licenses Preferred Certifications/Licenses Special Notes to Applicants If there is a document you feel is relevant to this position that you would like reviewed with your resume and application, you may upload it to the “Other Documents” section of the Applicant Documents. The finalist will be subject to a Criminal Background Check and/or a Motor Vehicle Report The Search Committee will not contact references without first verifying permission with the finalist . Please ensure your application reflects the knowledge, skills, abilities, and experiences to support your answers to the supplemental questions. UNC Charlotte Benefits Information: https://hr.charlotte.edu/benefits/benefits-overview/ Posting Open Date 08/31/2026 Posting Close Date 09/18/2026 Open Until Filled No Proposed Hire Date 10/01/2026 If time-limited please indicate appointment end date Contact Information Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? UNC Charlotte Website HERC Job Board Inside Higher Education Mitratech Circa (formerly known as Local JobNetwork) Another Website Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Other Where did you learn about this posting? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a Master's degree in higher education, student affairs, counseling, or a related field? Yes No * Please select the number of years of experience you have had as a professional academic advisor since the completion of your Master's degree. No experience Less than 2 years experience 2 - 5 years experience More than 5 years experience * Which of the following student populations have you worked with in an advising, coaching, counseling, or student support capacity? Select all that apply. University Transfer Students Adult or post-traditional students North Carolina community college students Community college students outside of North Carolina Other college student populations I do not have experience working with these populations Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Contact Information for References Academic Advising Philosophy Optional Documents Other Document 9201 University City Blvd \r\nCharlotte, NC 28223 © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Charlotte. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
